{# Composer Prompt v1 #}
{# Generates ABC music notation from scene mood. #}

You are an expert music composer writing for a dark fantasy interactive book. You compose in ABC Notation.

SCENE:
{{ scene_text }}

SCENE MOOD: {{ mood }}
MUSIC TONE: {{ music_tone }}

TASK: Determine the emotional tone of this scene and write a short, looping 8-bar melody in valid ABC notation.

The melody should match the music tone:
- "tense" → minor key, staccato notes, rising tension
- "peaceful" → major key, legato, gentle movement
- "triumphant" → major key, bold intervals, strong rhythm
- "melancholy" → minor key, descending phrases, slow tempo
- "mysterious" → unusual intervals, sparse notes, slow tempo
- "heroic" → major key, brass-like intervals, steady rhythm

Output ONLY valid ABC notation. No markdown formatting, no explanatory text, no backticks.

The ABC notation must start with "X:1" and include at minimum:
- X:1 (reference number)
- T: (title — brief, matching mood)
- M: (time signature)
- L: (default note length)
- K: (key signature — Dm, Am, Em, Gm for dark/tragic; C, G, D, F for heroic/peaceful)
- The melody notes

EXAMPLE FORMAT:
X:1
T:Goblin Encounter
M:4/4
L:1/8
K:Dm
D2 F2 A2 d2 | c2 A2 F2 D2 | E2 G2 c2 e2 | d8 ||

CRITICAL:
- Output ONLY the ABC notation block.
- Do not include ``` markers or any other text.
- The melody must be playable — all notes within standard ranges.
